From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:43:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 38/38] drm/imagination: apple: Keep reclaim out of the job
 worker

Memory pressure can stall a scheduler worker while its job fence is
needed to make memory reclaimable. Prepare S8003 PM resources in submit
ioctl context, before VM locks and arming. Take scene sets there, allocate
and persistently vmap aux buffers and pending pool growth outside the
worker's submit_lock, then publish pointers under that lock. Keep an
active set's old pool until the worker selects the idle set. The worker
only installs pre-reserved capacity and writes the existing records.
Missing capacity fails cleanly instead of allocating in the worker.

Allocation audit of run_job through chip submission:
- Shared submit_compute_job: fence allocation becomes GFP_NOWAIT.
- Shared submit_render_job (T8010): fence and translated command buffer
  become GFP_NOWAIT, retaining existing -ENOMEM cleanup.
- Shared submit_job (S8003): fence allocation becomes GFP_NOWAIT.
- S8003 pm_build: aux GEM creation, reserved VM mapping, pool creation
  and pool/aux vmaps move to prepare_job. Persistent maps make zeroing
  allocation-free. Replaced pools are released only when their set idles.
- S8003 job_write/fill and T8010 write_compute/write_geom/write_frag
  allocate nothing. Firmware restart reuses the initialized image/pages;
  the T8010 coherent window/heap and S8003 image are init-time allocations.

Publish PM set readiness only after aux mappings and pool resources exist.
Arming counts ready sets under set_lock and the worker selects them under
submit_lock; both locks protect readiness publication.

Only ioctl preparers take prepare_lock. No worker lock is held while
allocating the new resources. PM record format and sizing are unchanged.

Affects: Apple A9 and A10

Assisted-by: LLM
